- Story & Context: Long after the Ostrava foundries cooled into permanent silence, scavengers exploring the lower vaults discovered a single recording tape resting on a mound of calcified lace and brass filings. The tape contained only the echo of a single tenor saxophone weeping through a distortion pedal, accompanied by the rhythm of a cooling fan scraping against its housing. Local legend says that if you press your ear against the cold iron water pipes of the lower city, you can still hear the lingering question of the last unit ever brought offline. "Tell me if my skin is hard enough to touch the day."
